  steps:
    1. Pick period P in [3,6] and grid 5x15 with bg=0
    2. Pick K active rows (2-3) anchored at the bottom of the grid
    3. Build a P-wide tile column by column; bottom row gets all P cols filled;
       each row above gets a (strict or equal) subset of columns from the row below;
       row fg counts must be non-decreasing top-to-bottom
    4. Assign 2-3 distinct non-zero colors to tile cells; each column uses one color
    5. Tile the full 15-col output by repeating the P-wide tile
    6. Choose a cutoff C in [P+1, min(2*P+2, 14)] so input shows >=1 full repeat plus partial
    7. Input = output with columns C..14 replaced by background
